+
+Protocol 5 adds an explicit native request queue for functional checks in a
+reserved, private, single-player QA world. It creates no requests automatically.
+Build the agent into a fresh output directory; its manifest records protocol 5.
+A running v4 or older agent cannot be upgraded or sent these requests. Use a
+new launch/evidence label with the rebuilt agent and an explicit `--world` or
+`--fresh-world` whose name starts with `ATM9Qa`. The launch must use integrated
+mode and an offline QA player name beginning `ATM9Qa`.
+
+Only after the coordinator explicitly chooses the individual check, it may
+write a request such as:
+
+```powershell
+dotnet $qa native-command $fixture --label quickplay-02 --id 001-verity-item --world ATM9QaFresh --text 'give @s verity:verity_item'
+# Wait for the matching native_request_executed event before the next explicit request.
+dotnet $qa native-chat $fixture --label quickplay-02 --id 002-russian-chat --world ATM9QaFresh --text 'Верити, ответь по-русски: как тебя зовут?'
