+The CLI writes one atomic JSON file of at most 4096 bytes, with a safe unique ID
+and the exact launch world/UUID. Plain chat permits at most 256 UTF-16 code units
+and rejects slashes, controls and line breaks. The sole allowed command grammar
+is `give @s namespace:item` with an optional amount from 1 through 64; other
+selectors, commands, NBT, trailing arguments and separators are rejected.
+
+After three consecutive healthy joined-world observations, the agent checks the
+actual world name, offline player UUID, native in-memory connection, unpublished
+integrated server and exactly one matching server player. It repeats these checks
+immediately before ordinary `ClientPacketListener.sendChat`/`sendCommand`, using
+the verified 1.20.1 SRG methods. Unknown, public or multiplayer state refuses the
+request. No GUI/button/input path or packet constructor is synthesized. The
+native author chat handler receives the same ordinary player chat event.
+
+Each request is persistently claimed before dispatch, then records execution,
+refusal or failure. A claimed ID is never automatically retried, even after
+failure or worker restart. Repeating an identical CLI request preserves its
+original bytes; reusing its ID with different content fails. An execution event
+only proves that the native call returned; it does not prove the server effect,
+AI response, voice output or visual behavior. Those need separate observations.
